From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:42:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] /model refuses a concrete pin the managed routing
 registry rejects, and the rejection names it

Under model_routing.enforce_subscription_only a /model or Desktop-picker switch to a model the host's
registry lacks was saved (on the current provider the credential step swallowed the resolver's
ManagedPinRejectedError), then every later turn failed with 'Managed subscription policy rejects
unregistered or ambiguous concrete pin', naming neither the model nor the allowed pins.

- ManagedPinRejectedError's text now names the model, provider and allowed pins, and the way out
  (/model, or this host's model_routing.routes). Class, .allowed and .registry_empty unchanged.
- switch_model runs pin_policy on the name it would persist before credentials (new sibling
  hermes_cli/model_switch_managed.py). Class selectors and hosts without the policy are unchanged.

Self-heal defect agent-27ae0dbd84 (card t_01a1d4e458172558); repeat of t_01a1c68c9c1c515e.
